WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.840
Back to the P C L five flask

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.560
from earlier.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.480
Suppose we seal 0.40 moles of P C

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
L five into a 2.0 litre flask and

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.080
heat it, and this time we measure just

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.240
one thing.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.560
Chlorine is yellow-green, so its colour tells us

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.280
how much is there, and at equilibrium it

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.800
reads 0.080 moles per litre.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.760
Can we work out the other two concentrations

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.320
from it, and then the equilibrium constant?

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:32.173
This is an I C E table, spelled

00:00:32.414 --> 00:00:36.653
I, C, E, for initial, change and equilibrium.

00:00:37.214 --> 00:00:39.213
It has a column for each substance and

00:00:39.294 --> 00:00:41.533
a row for each of those three stages.

00:00:42.094 --> 00:00:44.173
We fill the initial row first.

00:00:44.494 --> 00:00:48.893
K uses concentrations, not moles, so divide: 0.40

00:00:49.054 --> 00:00:53.773
moles over 2.0 litres is 0.20

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:56.413
moles per litre of P C L five,

00:00:56.494 --> 00:00:58.573
and the two products start at zero.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:00.920
Now the change row.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.120
We know chlorine rose from zero to 0.080,

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.240
so its change is plus 0.080.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.360
How much did the others change?

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.080
Each P C L five that splits makes

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.880
one P C L three and one chlorine.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.000
So P C L three also rises by

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.400
0.080, and P C L five falls by

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:29.320
0.080, because one is used up for every

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.560
chlorine made.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.040
The change row follows the coefficients in the

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:33.720
equation.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.520
A substance used up gets a minus sign

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.160
and a substance made gets a plus.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:43.406
The equilibrium row is the initial row plus

00:01:43.487 --> 00:01:44.766
the change row.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:49.406
P C L five: 0.20 plus the change,

00:01:49.487 --> 00:01:53.926
minus 0.080, is 0.12.

00:01:54.287 --> 00:01:57.966
P C L three and chlorine are 0.080

00:01:58.207 --> 00:01:58.766
each.

00:01:59.967 --> 00:02:00.566
Now K.

00:02:00.607 --> 00:02:04.846
Products over reactants, with every coefficient one: K

00:02:05.007 --> 00:02:07.966
equals P C L three times chlorine, over

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:09.486
P C L five.

00:02:09.727 --> 00:02:14.526
Substitute the equilibrium values: 0.080 times

00:02:14.607 --> 00:02:18.286
0.080, over 0.12.

00:02:18.527 --> 00:02:24.446
The top is 0.0064, and 0.0064 divided

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:29.086
by 0.12 is 0.0533,

00:02:29.207 --> 00:02:33.526
so K is 0.053 to two significant figures.

00:02:33.727 --> 00:02:38.846
Check the subtraction: 0.12 plus 0.080 is

00:02:38.927 --> 00:02:41.566
0.20, what we started with.

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.046
Now the other way round.

00:02:44.447 --> 00:02:46.686
We know K and the start, and want

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.366
the settled concentrations.

00:02:49.007 --> 00:02:51.326
This is the hot hydrogen and iodine tube

00:02:51.407 --> 00:02:54.206
from the catalyst and expressions videos, where K

00:02:54.287 --> 00:02:55.326
is 49.

00:02:55.967 --> 00:02:59.566
Each dot is 0.05 moles per litre, so

00:02:59.647 --> 00:03:02.526
the start is 0.45 moles per litre of

00:03:02.607 --> 00:03:07.886
hydrogen, 0.45 of iodine and no hydrogen iodide.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.740
We don't know how much reacts, so call

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:14.380
the amount of hydrogen used up x, in

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.500
moles per litre.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.940
The equation, H two plus I two making

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.860
two H I, gives the rest.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:24.460
For each hydrogen used, one iodine is used

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.100
and two hydrogen iodide are made.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.460
So the change row is minus x, minus

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.540
x and plus two x.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:37.606
The equilibrium row is initial plus change: 0.45

00:03:37.687 --> 00:03:41.766
minus x for hydrogen and for iodine, and

00:03:41.927 --> 00:03:43.846
two x for hydrogen iodide.

00:03:44.407 --> 00:03:45.686
Substitute into K.

00:03:46.247 --> 00:03:49.846
Hydrogen iodide squared is two x all squared,

00:03:50.007 --> 00:03:53.446
over hydrogen times iodine, and both of those

00:03:53.607 --> 00:03:57.126
are 0.45 minus x, so the bottom is

00:03:57.287 --> 00:04:00.646
0.45 minus x, all squared.

00:04:00.727 --> 00:04:02.566
That equals 49.

00:04:02.647 --> 00:04:04.326
The top is squared and the bottom is

00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:07.446
squared, so the whole fraction is squared: two

00:04:07.527 --> 00:04:11.606
x over 0.45 minus x, all squared, equals

00:04:11.687 --> 00:04:12.886
49.

00:04:13.047 --> 00:04:15.926
Something squared equals a square number, a perfect

00:04:16.007 --> 00:04:19.206
square, and 49 is seven squared.

00:04:19.287 --> 00:04:21.766
So take the square root of both sides:

00:04:21.847 --> 00:04:25.926
two x over 0.45 minus x equals seven.

00:04:26.047 --> 00:04:29.366
Hydrogen iodide and hydrogen are both positive, so

00:04:29.447 --> 00:04:32.006
this ratio is positive and we keep plus

00:04:32.087 --> 00:04:32.566
seven.

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:34.966
Now rearrange.

00:04:35.447 --> 00:04:39.926
Multiply both sides by 0.45 minus x: two

00:04:40.007 --> 00:04:44.326
x equals 7 times 0.45 minus x, which

00:04:44.407 --> 00:04:47.046
is 3.15 minus 7x.

00:04:47.527 --> 00:04:50.406
Add 7x to both sides, so nine x

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:52.486
equals 3.15.

00:04:52.727 --> 00:04:53.686
Find x.

00:04:53.927 --> 00:04:55.366
Pause here and try it.

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:08.406
x is 0.35.

00:05:08.487 --> 00:05:12.806
So hydrogen and iodine are each 0.45 minus

00:05:12.887 --> 00:05:17.846
0.35, 0.10 moles per litre, and hydrogen

00:05:18.007 --> 00:05:23.206
iodide is two times 0.35, 0.70.

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:29.286
Check by substituting back: 0.70 squared is 0.49,

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:35.526
over 0.10 times 0.10, which is 0.010,

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.126
gives 49.

00:05:37.207 --> 00:05:38.806
Why not minus seven?

00:05:38.887 --> 00:05:42.246
That would need x of 0.63, more than

00:05:42.327 --> 00:05:45.606
the 0.45 we started with, so hydrogen would

00:05:45.687 --> 00:05:46.486
be negative.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:48.900
Here is the habit.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.740
Only the change row follows the coefficients: minus

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:58.660
0.35, minus 0.35 and plus 0.70 are

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.220
in the ratio one, one, two.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.100
The initial and equilibrium rows do not have

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:08.820
to be in that ratio: 0.10, 0.10 and

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.900
0.70 are not.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.100
K belongs to the equation as it is

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:14.580
written.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:20.340
Take the same settled tube, 0.10, 0.10 and

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:24.820
0.70, and write the equation backwards: two H

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.580
I making hydrogen plus iodine.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.980
K is now hydrogen times iodine over H

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:35.700
I squared: 0.10 times 0.10, over

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:41.860
0.70 squared, is 0.010 over 0.49,

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:47.060
about 0.020, and that is one over 49.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.380
Flip the equation, flip K.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:52.980
Double every coefficient and every power doubles, so

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:57.620
K is squared: 49 squared is 2401.

00:06:58.834 --> 00:06:59.473
Your turn.

00:07:00.034 --> 00:07:04.193
Dinitrogen tetroxide, N two O four, splits into

00:07:04.274 --> 00:07:06.593
nitrogen dioxide, N O two.

00:07:07.154 --> 00:07:10.833
We seal 0.100 moles of N two O

00:07:10.914 --> 00:07:14.433
four, and nothing else, in a 2.00 litre

00:07:14.514 --> 00:07:17.633
vessel at a steady temperature, and at equilibrium

00:07:17.874 --> 00:07:22.193
the concentration of N O two is 0.0300

00:07:22.354 --> 00:07:24.033
moles per litre.

00:07:24.194 --> 00:07:26.753
One: find K for N two O four

00:07:26.994 --> 00:07:29.233
making two N O two.

00:07:29.394 --> 00:07:31.793
Two: what is K for the equation written

00:07:31.874 --> 00:07:34.513
the other way, two N O two making

00:07:34.674 --> 00:07:36.913
N two O four, at the same temperature?

00:07:37.394 --> 00:07:38.673
Pause here to answer.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:49.740
One.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:54.700
Start with concentrations: 0.100 moles over

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.820
2.00 litres is 0.0500 moles

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:01.100
per litre.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:05.180
N O two rose by 0.0300, and the

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.420
equation makes two N O two for each

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:09.900
N two O four, so N two O

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:14.540
four fell by half of that, 0.0150.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:19.420
Equilibrium N two O four is 0.0500 minus

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:24.700
0.0150, 0.0350.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.020
K is N O two squared over N

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:34.700
two O four: 0.0300 squared is 0.000900,

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:40.700
over 0.0350, gives 0.0257.

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:43.980
If you got about 0.018, you used the

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:50.940
starting 0.0500 instead of the equilibrium 0.0350.

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:54.220
If you got 0.045, you took off the

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.260
whole 0.0300 instead of half of it.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.020
And if you got about 0.86, you forgot

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.460
to square the N O two.

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:04.066
Two.

00:09:04.347 --> 00:09:08.066
Written backwards, K is the old value flipped,

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:12.146
so it is one over 0.0257, which is

00:09:12.307 --> 00:09:13.986
38.9.

00:09:14.067 --> 00:09:16.706
The expression is N two O four over

00:09:16.787 --> 00:09:18.546
N O two squared.

00:09:18.627 --> 00:09:22.706
If you wrote 0.0257 again, check the direction

00:09:22.747 --> 00:09:25.306
of the equation: the products are now the

00:09:25.427 --> 00:09:26.546
N two O four.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:29.686
So when a question gives a start and

00:09:29.847 --> 00:09:32.966
one settled value, write the expression, put the

00:09:33.047 --> 00:09:36.006
concentrations in the initial row, fill the change

00:09:36.127 --> 00:09:38.486
row by the coefficients, add to get the

00:09:38.567 --> 00:09:41.846
equilibrium row, then substitute and check.

00:09:42.167 --> 00:09:44.566
When it gives K instead, call the change

00:09:44.727 --> 00:09:46.966
x, substitute and solve.

00:09:47.607 --> 00:09:49.446
That works in a clean way here because

00:09:49.527 --> 00:09:51.766
hydrogen and iodine started equal.

00:09:52.327 --> 00:09:54.166
Other starts give an equation that needs a

00:09:54.247 --> 00:09:56.006
different method, which comes later.

00:09:56.727 --> 00:10:00.566
Next: why factories do not wait for equilibrium.

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.126
Here are the key notes.

00:10:03.367 --> 00:10:05.206
Pause the video if you need more time

00:10:05.287 --> 00:10:06.086
to copy them.
